# ---------------------------------------------------------------- data ----
# The atlas and the external cohorts are shared as data, not committed: they are large, and
# `data/external/beataml/norm_exp.txt` alone is 281 MB — well past what GitHub will accept.
# Fetch BeatAML2 from https://github.com/biodev/beataml2.0_data ; the atlas from the lab archive.
*.h5ad
data/

# Uploaded / synthesised test samples (regenerate: pipeline/make_upload_test_sample.py)
inbox/

# --------------------------------------------------------------- models ----
# Committed: bulk_mutation_predictor.pkl (4 MB), drug_response_model.pkl (14 MB), control_gate.pkl.
# Excluded: the multimodal single-cell predictors, which are 124–152 MB — over GitHub's hard limit.
# Rebuild with pipeline/train_predictor.py.
pipeline/mutation_predictor*.pkl

# Regenerable cache blocks (_sl_Cell-comm.pkl alone is 212 MB)
runs/single_modality/_sl_*.pkl

# --------------------------------------------------- generated artefacts ----
# The static export is fully regenerable: python pipeline/build_static_site.py
deliverables/mosaic_static/
deliverables/*.zip

# ------------------------------------------------------------ python/OS ----
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.DS_Store
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.env
